  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;be three statements such that the truth value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math> .&nbsp;Then the truth values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;are respectively :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>F</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>F</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given that the truth value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;.</p><p>For the above truth value to be possible,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;should be TRUE and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;should be FALSE.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is TRUE when&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;both are TRUE.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is FALSE when&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;is TRUE and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;is FALSE.</p><p>So, the truth values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively.</p>"
  }
